movies |&gt;
  group_by(studio) |&gt;
  summarize(n = n()) |&gt;
  arrange(desc(n)) |&gt;
  head(1)

#&gt; # A tibble: 1 × 2
#&gt;   studio                 n
#&gt;   &lt;chr&gt;              &lt;int&gt;
#&gt; 1 Paramount Pictures    37

Interaction 1: predict

movies |&gt;
  group_by(genre) |&gt;
  summarize(avg_runtime = mean(runtime))


Turn to your neighbor (2 min): how many rows? Will any value be NA?


INTERACTION 1 of 3. Take 2 minutes, then reveal on the next slide. Answer: 11 rows (one per genre). Documentary shows NA because one documentary, “The End of America”, has a missing runtime, and mean() of anything containing NA is NA.

na.rm: decide on purpose

movies |&gt;
  group_by(genre) |&gt;
  summarize(
    avg_runtime = mean(runtime, na.rm = TRUE),
    na_dropped = sum(is.na(runtime))
  ) |&gt;
  filter(genre == "Documentary")

#&gt; # A tibble: 1 x 3
#&gt;   genre       avg_runtime na_dropped
#&gt;   &lt;chr&gt;             &lt;dbl&gt;      &lt;int&gt;
#&gt; 1 Documentary        96.5          1


na.rm = TRUE ignores missing values. Use it knowingly, and say how many were dropped.

Read a whole pipeline aloud

movies |&gt;
  filter(title_type == "Feature Film") |&gt;
  group_by(genre) |&gt;
  summarize(n = n(), avg_score = mean(audience_score)) |&gt;
  filter(n &gt;= 20) |&gt;
  arrange(desc(avg_score))

#&gt; # A tibble: 5 x 3
#&gt;   genre                  n avg_score
#&gt;   &lt;chr&gt;              &lt;int&gt;     &lt;dbl&gt;
#&gt; 1 Drama                301      65.3
#&gt; 2 Mystery & Suspense    59      55.9
#&gt; 3 Action & Adventure    65      53.8
#&gt; 4 Comedy                85      51.8
#&gt; 5 Horror                23      45.8



Say it out loud with the class: filter, group, summarize, filter the groups, sort.

Raw names are messy

movies |&gt;
  count(studio) |&gt;
  filter(str_detect(studio, "(?i)warner")) |&gt;
  arrange(studio) |&gt;
  head(5)

#&gt; # A tibble: 5 x 2
#&gt;   studio                       n
#&gt;   &lt;chr&gt;                    &lt;int&gt;
#&gt; 1 WARNER BROTHERS PICTURES     9
#&gt; 2 Warner Bros Pictures         1
#&gt; 3 Warner Bros.                 7
#&gt; 4 Warner Bros. Pictures       30
#&gt; 5 Warner Home Video           19


Many spellings. The lookup maps four to Warner Bros.

Unmatched rows become NA

movies |&gt;
  left_join(studios, by = "studio") |&gt;
  count(studio_group, sort = TRUE) |&gt;
  head(4)

#&gt; # A tibble: 4 x 2
#&gt;   studio_group     n
#&gt;   &lt;chr&gt;        &lt;int&gt;
#&gt; 1 &lt;NA&gt;           249
#&gt; 2 Warner Bros.    82
#&gt; 3 Paramount       58
#&gt; 4 Sony            58


249 films have no group. The lookup does not know their studio.

Join, then summarize

movies |&gt;
  left_join(studios, by = "studio") |&gt;
  filter(!is.na(studio_group)) |&gt;
  summarize(n = n(), avg_score = mean(audience_score), .by = studio_group) |&gt;
  arrange(desc(avg_score)) |&gt;
  head(5)

#&gt; # A tibble: 5 x 3
